From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Subject: [PATCH] alsactl: skip controls another process has locked

A control locked by another process (SNDRV_CTL_IOCTL_ELEM_LOCK) can only
be written by its owner, so restoring it fails with EPERM and alsactl
logged "Cannot write control ... Operation not permitted" for each one.
On Apple Silicon Macs the speaker protection daemon locks the speaker
amplifier controls before alsa-restore runs, which gave about 25 errors
per boot. Treat a control locked by someone else like a read-only one
and leave it to its owner.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
--- a/alsactl/state.c
+++ b/alsactl/state.c
@@ -1427,6 +1427,10 @@
 
 	if (snd_ctl_elem_info_is_inactive(info) ||
 				!snd_ctl_elem_info_is_writable(info))
+		return 0;
+	/* A control another process has locked is that process's to set. */
+	if (snd_ctl_elem_info_is_locked(info) &&
+	    !snd_ctl_elem_info_is_owner(info))
 		return 0;
 	snd_ctl_elem_value_set_numid(ctl, snd_ctl_elem_id_get_numid(elem_id1));
 
